<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marcist Revolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1845</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Marcist Revolution was an uprising that began in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guayaquil">Guayaquil</a> on 6 March 1845 against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-jose-flores">Juan José Flores</a>, the Venezuelan-born general who had dominated Ecuador since its foundation in 1830. Led by Guayaquil merchants and liberals, it forced Flores to leave the country. Its name comes from the month of March, and it began a period of civilian government by coastal elites.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marcist-revolution.jpg" alt="Marcist Revolution" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Orange Tuesday at English Wikipedia (Original text: Orange Tuesday (talk)) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Ecuador_(1845).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
